    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get the \"hybrid\" thing, but that feels like a safe, middle-of-the-road answer for an AI. In a real legal philosophy debate, you can't just waffle. If you look at the actual moral goals of a just society today—empathy, reducing recidivism, and addressing systemic inequality—doesn't that make the restorative framework objectively more aligned with modern ethics than the old-school retributive model? Or are you saying it's actually equal?",
